WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:01.480
You are...!

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.980
III!

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.860
But now I'll fight alongside you as a friend!

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.690
Duel!!

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.200
So that's his...

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.660
...true form!

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.530
I'll take the first turn!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.120
My turn! Draw!

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.720
I can't stand things that take too long!

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:31.210
So we'll go with the rule in this Tag Duel 
that I can attack in the first turn!

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.550
What gives you the right?!

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.980
I Summon Oily Cicada!

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.150
I then Special Summon Suiminmin the Dream Cicada!

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.670
I can Special Summon this guy when I've got a face-up Attack Position Insect-Type Monster on the field,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:57.140
and and I can change one Insect-Type Monster to Defense Position!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.990
I'll change Oily Cicada to Defense Position!

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.150
When Oily Cicada's Battle Position changes,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.310
it can be used as two Xyz Materials!

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.090
He's gonna do it?!

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.670
I'll Overlay my Level Three Oily Cicada twins and Suiminmin!

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.480
I'll use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.440
Xyz Summon!

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.280
Show yourself, Number 3!

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.790
Did he say Number 3?!

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:26.910
That's right!

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.590
This is the Number I got from Lord Vector in order to bury you fools!

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:38.180
III, I could care less what you call yourself! The true Number 3's my Number!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.580
After years of slumber, 
sing loudly your victory from the depths of Hell!

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.850
Hell Cicada Emperor - Locust King!

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.350
So that's his Number!

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.200
But in Defense Mode?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.130
He was saying he'd attack in the first turn...

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.780
Yuma... You can't let your guard down.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.970
I'm sure he's planning something.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.400
I'll set two cards and end my turn!

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.570
<i>Yuma... Even without Astral, this Duel is a huge ordeal for you...</i>

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.900
<i>In order to ensure you can overcome it and stand back on your feet...</i>

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.900
<i>I have come here!</i>

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:44.740
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.790
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:55.250
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.800
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.680
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:10.020
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.230
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.110
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:20.740
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.820
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:32.290
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.540
My turn! Draw!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.250
<i>Double Up Chance!</i>

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:57.960
<i>I used this card in combo with Hope
 during the first Duel I met Astral in.</i>

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.970
<i>Fighting together, we always continued looking forward.</i>

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.640
<i>Even if I'm alone, I have to continue looking forward!</i>

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.890
"The Power of a New Hope!!
 Combination of Friendship - "Atlantal Hope""

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.100
What's wrong? Have you given up
 all hope now that Astral isn't here?

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.900
Shut up, fly bastard!

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.110
Flies are supposed to buzz and annoy people!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.570
I Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.040
Then I Special Summon Kagetokage!

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:36.290
This guy can be Special Summoned when I successfully Summon a Level Four or lower Monster!

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.590
<i>Astral, watch me...!</i>

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.340
I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Magician and Kagetokage!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.930
I build the Overlay Network with these two Monsters!

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.560
Xyz Summon!

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.690
Show yourself, Number 39! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.280
Played it right from the start, eh?

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:04.780
<i>Astral...</i>

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.660
No...! I have to focus on the Duel now!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:17.670
I then activate the Quick-Play Spell from my hand, Quick Reservation Reward

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:23.630
This card allows me to reveal a Quick-Play Spell from my hand to the opponent and then set it!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.050
I set Double Up Chance!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.470
Double Up Chance?

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.350
The card set by the effect of Quick Reservation Reward

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.310
can be activated this turn, and the Monster that uses its effect

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.060
has its Attack Power doubled during a battle.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.440
And when it attacks a Defense Position Monster,

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.360
and its Attack Power is higher than its Defense Power,

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.740
the opponent receives damage equal to the same amount!

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:54.580
<i>I see. Yuma's trying to negate the battle using Hope</i>

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.500
<i>which will activate Double Up Chance</i>

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.000
<i>and then Hope can attack with its Attack Power doubled.</i>

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.960
<i>And using the effect of Quick Reservation Reward along with it,</i>

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.130
<i>he can then double its Attack Power again!</i>

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.220
<i>If this works, it'll deal a huge chunk of damage worth 7500 points!</i>

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.850
<i>What a nice combo, Yuma!</i>

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.730
<i>As I figured, thanks to Astral's guidance,</i>

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.730
<i>you've grown as a Duelist.</i>

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.110
<i>And now that you've lost Astral, you're moving forward.</i>

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:28.910
I... I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope to attack Locust King!

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.370
At this moment, I detach one Overlay Unit

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.620
and negate Hope's own attack!

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.710
And then I-

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.830
I won't let you!

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:46.510
I detach one Overlay Unit in order to activate Locust King's effect!

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.130
When the opponent's Monster activates an effect,

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.890
it negates that Monster's effect!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.800
Memory Sucker!

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:54.640
What?!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.140
Now the effect you just used is negated!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.350
Then, thanks to this effect,

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.900
I raise Locust King's Defense Power up by 500 points!

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.360
3000 Defense Points?!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.610
So this is why he played it in Defense Mode!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.450
Too bad!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.910
Since the battle wasn't negated,

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.500
your Magic Card won't activate!

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:23.080
So the battle continues with its Attack Points as is!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.130
Yuma!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.260
It's okay! This is nothing!

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.260
I'll end my turn with that!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.350
You have my condolences for those 500 Life Points you lost in vein.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:45.110
Even if he tries his best, a fool is still a fool.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:50.650
It means that without Astral, he's nothing but a trashy Duelist.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.370
<i>Yuma, you aren't alone.</i>

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.530
<i>Now that you've lost Astral</i>

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.370
<i>the bonds you've forged with others through your Duels</i>

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.750
<i>will definitely unleash an enormous power!</i>

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.080
<i>I'll be certain to make you realize that.</i>

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.460
<i>This is something I must do no matter what.</i>

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:12.130
<i>Because in the past, I also took Astral away from you!</i>

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.850
My turn! Draw!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.020
I Special Summon OOPArts Moai Carrier!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:25.770
When I have no Monsters on the field, this card can be Special Summoned.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:29.230
Continuing, I Special Summon OOPArts Wings Sphinx!

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:35.280
When I have an OOPArts Monster on the field, this card can be Special Summoned!

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.990
Yuma, I'm using the power of the Numbers you gave me!

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:44.120
I Overlay the Level Five OOParts Moai Carrier and Wings Sphinx!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.880
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:50.960
Xyz Summon!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:09:00.720
Come out, Number 33! OOPArts Super Weapon - Machu Mach!

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.520
Wow, you got Machu Mach out!

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:08.810
Hmph! What can a Number that's just a giant pile of junk do?

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.360
Is it really junk?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.230
Find out with your own eyes!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:17.110
I activate the Continuous Spell from my hand, OOPArts Pyramid Eye Tablet!

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:27.250
This card raises the Attack Power of all OOPArts Monsters on my field by 800 points!

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.710
At this moment, Mashu Mach's effect activates!

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.630
When the Attack Points of Monsters on the field change,

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.840
I can detach one Overlay Unit and damage the opponent by

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.640
the same amount of points!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.980
Hey, III... His Monster...

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.940
That's right!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.190
Have you forgotten Locust King's effect?!

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:55.070
I detach one Overlay Unit in order to activate Locust King's effect!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.950
It negates the opponent's effects

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.490
and raises its Defense Power by 500!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.370
Memory Sucker!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.960
Now Mashu Mach lost all its memories!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:11.000
Tch, Locust King's Defense Power went up again!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:12.920
It's okay, Yuma.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.630
The card you left on the field

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.300
will guide me to victory!

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.090
Huh?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.470
I activate the effect of the Continuous Spell, Quick Reservation Reward!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:28.600
Using this card, I set Heart of Stone!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.770
Mashu Mach, attack Locust King!

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.690
What?! Why are you attacking Locust King?!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:43.620
III!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.170
Why would he do that knowing he'd take damage?!

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.000
Using the effect of Quick Reservation Reward,

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.800
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Heart of Stone!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.680
When an OOPArts Monster couldn't destroy the opponent's Monster in battle,

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.220
that Monster can attack once again!

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:12.650
Then, at this moment, thanks to the effect of Quick Reservation Reward,

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:15.520
Mashu Mach's Attack Power doubles!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.440
6400 Attack Points!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.910
I get it! III's aiming for that!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.330
Mashu Mach, attack Locust King once again!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.620
Fire of Vril!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.590
I won't let you! I activate the Continuous Trap, Cicada Mirage!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:45.760
It protects one Cicada Monster on my field from being destroyed in battle!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:46.640
What?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.520
But even if your Monster isn't destroyed,

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:55.480
you still take damage because of 
the effect of Quick Reservation Reward!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.190
Semimaru!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.400
He did it...

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.740
Have you learned your lesson? This is the power drawn from two friends fighting together!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.580
When the battle ends, Mashu Mach's Attack Power returns to normal.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:13.960
Damn brats...! You actually made me get serious!

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.000
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.420
My turn! Draw!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:25.390
I'll make you shitty little brats cry uncontrollably!

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.560
I switch Locust King into Attack Position!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:38.690
When Locust King is switched to Attack Position while being targeted by Cicada Mirage,

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.900
Cicada Mirage's other effect activates!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.120
Its 3500 Defense Points are added to its Attack Power!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.280
4700 Attack Points...!

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:53.290
I'd like to pay you back for that little stunt earlier, but first...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.460
I gotta make sure I beat the snot out of this one!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.380
I use Locust King to attack Hope!

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.340
If this goes through, you're finished!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.650
But it won't! Trap, activate!

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.360
Orichalcum Mirage!

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.690
This card, when the opponent attacks,

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:25.780
changes the target to an OOPArts Monster on my field!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.410
III!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.340
You just had to interfere!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.670
III, you okay?! III!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.380
I-I'm fine.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:51.060
But why... Why did you...?!

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.720
Yuma, I told you...

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:57.940
That I'd become your sword and your shield...

00:13:59.190 --> 00:13:59.900
III...

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.070
So you plan to save your friend?

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.740
Your loss is as good as decided now!

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:11.870
What?!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.700
I activate the Continuous Trap, Cicada Final!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:19.380
This card activates when I damage the opposing player!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:22.670
That 1500 damage you took just now,

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:26.130
once I send this card to the Graveyard on my next turn,

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.760
will be inflicted on you both once again!

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:34.180
This is the final stage for the both of you!

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:38.940
I then set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.530
<i>Me and III will lose when his next turn comes...!</i>

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.860
My turn! Draw!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.870
<i>There has to be a way to deal with him...</i>

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.990
<i>These cards have to...</i>

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.620
<i>He's racking his brain, but it's useless!</i>

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:04.290
<i>I have my set card, Cicada Chirp Force.</i>

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:11.090
<i>It activates when I receive an attack 
while I control a Cicada Monster.</i>

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:14.600
<i>It destroys all face-up Monsters they have!</i>

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.480
<i>It's no use...! My current hand...!</i>

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:21.650
Yuma...

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.520
Yuma-<i>kun</i>...

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.400
You can do it, or not...

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.030
Yuma...

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:29.530
Yuma...

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:30.950
Guys!

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:31.700
Impossible!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:36.240
All their memories were supposed to be stolen, so why?!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:38.950
Because they're his friends!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.420
Back to playing your pretend friendship, huh?

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.090
Shut up! Even if their memories were taken,

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.880
the feelings they have for their friend 
carved in their souls won't change!

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:52.130
<i>Guys...</i>

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.640
That's right... I still have...

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.600
Yuma... You can do it...

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.440
<i>I still have my friends!</i>

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.360
I'll fight along with my friends!

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:12.320
III, I'm lending Hope to you.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:13.320
Huh?!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.080
I activate the Magic Card, Release Reverse Burst!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.950
It sends an Xyz Monster I control to the Graveyard,

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:25.830
and destroys all the Magic and Trap Cards set on my opponent's field!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.000
What?!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:28.800
The one I'm sending to the Graveyard is...

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.720
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.890
Damn...! My Trap...!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:42.560
But you'll both still lose some my next turn!

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:48.270
I then Special Summon Giragira Lancer from my hand onto III's field!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.650
When I have no Monsters on the field, this Monster

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.700
can be Special Summoned onto the opponent's field!

00:16:55.450 --> 00:17:00.290
But its effect will inflict 500 points of damage to III come the end of his turn,

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.700
and increase my Life by 500.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.790
Whoa there, III's only got 200 Life left.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.340
You trying to kill your friend in order to save yourself?

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:15.970
<i>This is my trump card to show I believe in my friends!</i>

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:20.010
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:26.520
So you'll sacrifice your friend in order to save yourself!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.690
Shut up!

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.940
Real friends aren't like that at all!

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.190
I'll prove that to you right now!

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.820
My turn! Draw!

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.370
<i>The card Yuma just set on his field...</i>

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.120
<i>If he's doing what I think he is...</i>

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.870
I activate the Continuous Spell, Orichalcum Chain, from my hand!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.420
When this card is on my field,

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:55.510
the next time I Summon an Xyz Monster, it can be Summoned with one less Xyz Material!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:57.380
Yuma, let's go!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.220
Yeah!

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:03.640
I Overlay the Level Six Giragira Lancer!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.560
I use this one Monster to build the Overlay Network!

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.400
Xyz Summon!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.860
Come forth, Number 6!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.070
OOPArts, Atlantal!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:27.000
When Atlantal is Summoned, I can equip one Number in the Graveyard to it,

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.290
and raise its Attack Power by its total Attack Points!

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.250
Revive, Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:40.300
I see! He uses Release Reverse Burst not to destroy my set card,

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.140
but to get Hope into the Graveyard!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:52.060
Behold! This is the light of hope emitted through the bonds forged by friends in battle!

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:58.110
And because of the effect of the Continuous Spell, Pyramid Eye Tablet,

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:01.820
it increases the Attack Power of an OOPArts Monster by 800!

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:07.080
But Locust King's Attack Power is 4700!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.500
I'll only take 1200 points of damage from a battle!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.290
You sure about that?

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.630
I attack Locust King with Atlantal!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.800
Trap, activate! Overlay Brake!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:28.230
This card negates the attack of one Xyz Monster on the field!

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.810
Negates the attack?!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.230
In order to grasp our true victory!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.570
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Double Up Chance!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:42.320
Dammit! The card resurrected that combo just now...!

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:45.950
When a Monster's attack is negated,

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.870
it doubles that Monster's Attack Points,

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.210
and also allows it to attack again!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:57.460
And I'll now activate the effect of the Continuous Spell, Quick Reservation Reward!

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.510
It doubles Atlantal's Attack Power once again!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.640
23600 Attack Points?!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.810
Atlantal, attack Locust King once again!

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:14.440
When the heritage of God harbors a light of hope beyond human intelligence,

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.360
judgment forged by the heat of bonds is dealt!

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.820
Go! This is the power of friendship!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.740
Hope Sword Cross Atlantal Slash!!

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.760
S-Semimaru!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.400
Yuma Tsukumo...!

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:03.820
We...

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:04.950
We...

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:06.070
What exactly...?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.990
To summarize, what...?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.450
Ah, Yuma!

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:11.540
You guys!

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.040
Yuma...

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.620
What are you doing here?

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.330
Are you guys okay?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.220
Thanks, guys.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:26.090
You guys definitely encouraged me.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:29.050
III.

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:33.560
I want you to take this as proof of our friendship.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:36.770
This is... Number 3.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.690
I was able to obtain this thanks to you.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:42.610
I understand.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.990
I'll look after the power of this Number.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.160
<i>Astral... Did you watch our Duel today?</i>

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:56.790
<i>I thought I was sad and useless without you here...</i>

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.420
<i>But I have friends. I can't stay depressed forever.</i>

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:07.510
<i>But still, Astral... I...</i>

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:23.650
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:26.190
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:27.400
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:28.820
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:31.700
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:34.200
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:36.750
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:37.830
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:38.870
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:44.590
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:47.720
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.930
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:52.930
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:54.890
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:56.270
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:58.140
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:02.440
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:07.530
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:08.780
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:12.780
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:18.160
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:19.370
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:23.500
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:25.670
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:27.880
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:43.060
Shark returns to the location of his past memories.

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:47.480
But he's lured into a Barian's trap and placed in danger.

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:51.910
But at that moment, none other than
 the presumptuous Duelist appears!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:55.490
I haven't been here since...that day...

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:56.950
Rio-<i>san</i>'s been poisoned!

00:23:57.120 --> 00:23:58.370
Shark's in danger!

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:00.870
I'm losing my strength...!

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:03.330
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:06.540
"Duelists of Sorrow - The Gimmick Puppets' Rumble of Darkness!!"

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:08.880
Why are you here?!
